1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
AbbeyRoad.online: a database and practice-scheduling tool
for a university band club.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A member logs in and opens "My Schedule",
where the Google Calendar integration is offered.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Integration is optional. The member clicks "Connect with Google".
A link to our privacy policy is shown next to the button.

4
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The Google consent screen shows the app name
and the client ID in the address bar.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Two scopes are requested: calendar.calendarlist.readonly
(list the user's calendars) and calendar.events (read and write events).

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The user explicitly allows access
and returns to the app.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Scope: calendar.calendarlist.readonly.
The app lists the calendars shown in the user's Google Calendar
and reads events only from those.

8
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Scope: calendar.events (read).
Busy times are removed from practice candidates.
Event titles are visible only to the user; others see only "busy".

9
00:02:25,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Scope: calendar.events (create).
When a practice date is decided, one event is added
to the user's own Google Calendar.

10
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Scope: calendar.events (update / delete).
Changing or cancelling the practice updates or removes only
the event created by this app.

11
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:40,000
The user can disconnect at any time.
This revokes the token and deletes the imported data.

12
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Our privacy policy explains how Google user data is used
and follows the Google API Services User Data Policy, including Limited Use.
